0x141a6dd60	FeTile_Clear_EraTileSet_Thunk	fe_tiles.clear_era_tile_set	L2	fe_tiles	void FeTile_Clear_EraTileSet_Thunk(void *tiles)	decomp:re/decomp/141a6dd60.c;decomp:re/decomp/153417330.c;decomp:re/decomp/141a6e980.c;xref:0x141a6eb62,0x141b432eb,0x141b435fb,0x141b4390b	5-byte jmp thunk into the .data1 body 0x14bd31910 (call only, never hook). Clears an era tile set laid out like view model+0x690: empties the list node held at tiles+0x8 through 0x14420cd60 (jmp 0x153417330), which for a list node calls 0x1442bc9c0(node, 0) until the node's child vector (+0x40..+0x48) is empty, unless the node's read-only bit +0x26&1 is set; destroys each {allocator, Tile*} entry of the vector [tiles+0x48, tiles+0x50) (Tile vt+0 with 0, then allocator vt+0x38), frees the vector buffer through the allocator at tiles+0x40, zeroes +0x48..+0x58, and unlinks and releases (0x1442b3d70) the node handles at tiles+0x28 and tiles+0x8. It writes the base vtable 0x145612e48 over +0x0 and +0x20 but calls no vtable of the set, so a set whose vector is empty only empties its list and releases its two nodes; +0x28 is zeroed through an obfuscated store (dword 0x1572a3004 + 0x3c50f0b8, 0 on this build). FeTile_Build_EraTiles calls it at 0x141a6eb62 on vm+0x690 when vm+0x6f0 is set, then writes its own vtables back. More callers, not read: 0x141b432eb in 0x141b43290, 0x141b435fb in 0x141b435a0, 0x141b4390b in 0x141b438b0, and from .data1 0x14bd36f70 (in 0x14bd36f40) and 0x14bddd9fe (in 0x14bddd9a0) (V1014).
0x141a6e420	FeTile_Press_EraTile	fe_tiles.press_era_tile	L2	fe_tiles	char *FeTile_Press_EraTile(void *view_model, void *command)	decomp:re/decomp/141a6e420.c;xref:0x14572a4f0,0x141a6e977;decomp:re/decomp/141a6e420.c	DynamicEraSelectTabViewModel command handler (vtable 0x14572a4a0 slot 10 at 0x14572a4f0, also via the adjustor thunk 0x141a6e970). On a tile press it reads the pressed index from the VM tiles node, takes the Tile from the vector at vm+0x6d8, reports dynamic_era_select_tile_pressed with the Tile's command (Tile+0x150) and raises entrant_list_selected with it; entrant_goto_select otherwise. Tiles added by FeTile_Add_EraTile after the stock ones are handled the same way. Raises entrant_list_selected only while vm+0x6f0 is set, the latch vm+0x708 is 0, the Tile is enabled (node at Tile+0xf0) and 0x1424283d0(*(vm+0x688), command, dynamic_era_select_tile_pressed) returns nonzero; the index comes from the tile node order under VM tiles and is not bounds-checked against the vector (V1005).
0x141a6e980	FeTile_Build_EraTiles	-	L2	fe_tiles	void FeTile_Build_EraTiles(void *view_model)	decomp:re/decomp/141a6e980.c;decomp:re/decomp/141a6d0e0.c;decomp:re/decomp/141a6cfd0.c;xref:0x14572a538	DynamicEraSelectTabViewModel (the Grand Prix, Time Trial and split-screen category boxes, VM dynamic_era_select) tile build, reached through the vtable 0x14572a4a0 slot 19 at 0x14572a538. Resets the VM tiles and selected_tile nodes, then adds a fixed list of tiles with FeTile_Add_EraTile, each behind FeTile_Is_EraScenarioAvailable_Thunk(*(vm+0x670), setup mode, entrant list): f1_preview/f1_2025_preview, f1_preview/f1_2025_esports_preview, f1_26/f1_2026 (image [f1_26], is_dlc), f1/f1_2025, f1/f1_2024 (image [f1]), f1_world (player_car image; the command comes from the scenario registry), 0000/0000, f2/f2_2026, f2/f2_2025, f2/f2_2024, f2/f2_2023. No database list drives the tiles: a game_setup.scenarios row only shows if one of these pairs names it. Ends at site_FeTile_EraTilesBuilt, then sets vm+0x6f0, posts the tab message and refreshes. The two preview tiles also need 0x14078dbe0(*(vm+0x678), *(vm+0x680), entrant list); f2_26 is is_dlc 1 too; f1_world is disabled and titled lng_not_available_in_preview while the byte at *(*0x1460fddb8+0x18) is set (V1004).
0x141a76130	Game_F1WorldActivityContainer_AddTabs	-	L2	game	void(void *container_vm)	decomp:re/decomp/141a76130.c;xref:0x141a762e7,0x141a7644a,0x141a7659a;kb:subsystems/vm.md#tabs	F1WorldActivityContainerViewModel builds its 7 tab VMs (ctor 0x1414bdac0 with the template name and the lng title) into the vector at vm+0x2c8, in this order: f1_world_activity (lng_f1_world_play), f1_world_activity_offline (lng_f1_world_play_offline), dynamic_era_select (lng_solo_grand_prix), public_gp_select (lng_public_grand_prix), dynamic_era_select (lng_time_trial), dynamic_era_select (lng_screen_era_select), session_create_dlc_select_tab (lng_create_session_dlc_select; template registered by f1_world_container.ui). No tab instantiates time_trial_select, which f1_world_activity_container.ui also registers (correction 2026-10-23: an earlier note listed it in place of session_create_dlc_select_tab). The UITC instantiates each tab template by name (Vm_UiTabs_OnMessage). Runtime-observed 2026-10-23 with re/tools/ui_trace (gdb, breaking and fixed era builds; logs not filed as a T### run, so not L3): the content loop built exactly these seven templates in this order. docs/reference/ui/engine.md
